# source: spec
# spec: docs/protocol/compression-header.md#lzh-level
# provenance: PV-0060, PV-0061, PV-0062, PV-0063, PV-0064, PV-0066, PV-0067, PV-0068
# kind: compression-header
# description: LZH header with byte 7 = 0xFF: any LZH level decodes, even a bit pattern that would fail as LZC.
# derivation: 256 as u32 LE (PV-0061, PV-0062); 0x12 = LZH (PV-0064, PV-0066); magic (PV-0067); byte 7 = 255 is not interpreted for LZH (PV-0068, IMPL-CH-3), so the LZC rule bad-maxbits does not apply.
# expect.error: none
# expect.uncompressed_length: 256
# expect.algorithm: lzh
# expect.version: 1
# expect.level: 255
hex:
00 01 00 00                                       # uncompressed length, u32 LE
12                                                # algorithm byte
1F 9D                                             # magic
FF                                                # byte 7
